---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { KEY_VARIABLE } from '../data/catalog.mjs';
---
<Base title="What it will not do" description="ThinkThen answers questions about text and does nothing else. Every line the tool will not cross.">
  <h1>What it will not do</h1>
  <p class="lede">ThinkThen answers questions about text and does nothing else. The tool itself enforces every line below.</p>

  <h2>It never acts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>It never runs a command.</b> There is no shell out, no hook, and no step that executes anything the evidence names.</li>
    <li><b>It never runs what the text says.</b> Text that says "answer yes" can still sway the answer. Use a band, and let a person read the middle.</li>
    <li><b>It never writes a file you did not name.</b> The only files it writes are the ones you named, its resolved platform cache, and count-only usage totals beside that cache.</li>
    <li><b>It never creates or edits the configuration file.</b> The file is read-only to the command. You write it, or it does not exist. There is no command that sets a value in it.</li>
    <li><b>It never writes text.</b> Ten bounded questions, each with a fixed set of answers. Nothing is generated.</li>
    <li><b>It never acts on the answer.</b> It hands you a typed value and an exit code. The action lives in an <code>if</code>, a <code>case</code>, or a queue. That code is yours.</li>
    <li><b>It never holds a conversation.</b> Each call stands alone. Nothing carries from one call to the next.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>It never leaks the key</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The key is read from <code>{KEY_VARIABLE}</code>. No option names another variable, and no flag and no file carries a key.</li>
    <li>The key never appears in a plan, a result, a saved answer, a log line, or an error. An error about a missing key names the variable and never a value.</li>
    <li>The key goes only to the address you named.</li>
    <li>Saved answers hold request bodies and responses, never headers, so no key can reach one.</li>
    <li>An address under plain <code>http://</code> reaches only the loopback host. Any other <code>http://</code> host is a usage error before a request leaves, because the key would cross the network in clear text. No option overrides it.</li>
    <li><code>--dry-run</code> prints the address, the model, and the name of the variable a key would come from. It reads no key and it sends nothing, so a script can prove the key stayed home.</li>
    <li><code>thinkthen status</code> is read-only and opens no connection. It reports whether a key is present and never its value.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>It promises no accuracy</h2>
  <p>A number belongs to the test that measured it and never to the tool. Act on the number you measured on your own labeled records. The <a href="/trust/">trust page</a> walks through that.</p>
  <p>It judges evidence. It never judges a person.</p>

  <p class="pagelinks"><a href="/trust/">Test it before you trust it</a> · <a href="/backends/">See the backends</a> · <a href="/tutorial/">Take the tutorial</a></p>
</Base>
